From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 11:54:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: the now-playing island always ends whole, and says when
 it did not

The now-playing island's show and hide animations and its title and
artwork fades now end in a known state however they stop. A show cut short
by anything but a hide still leaves the island opaque at its natural size,
and a hide cut short by anything but a show still hides it. A fade that is
stopped leaves the title or artwork opaque.

A guard (lumaMediaIslandGuard.js) checks the island about a second after it
last changed with nothing animating. If the island or its content is still
translucent, is held narrower than its content, has its controls hidden or
squeezed out, or carries an insensitive state it should not, the guard
writes one line to the journal and puts the island back: the opacity of each
part, the size against the natural size, style classes, pseudo-classes, the
title's font, the last show or hide and what stopped it, and the last fade.
It reports at most once a minute and counts the times in between. It does
nothing while anything on the island is animating, and costs nothing while
the island is hidden.
